/-!
# Residue degree of a canonical binary closed point

The residue field of chart evaluation is the subfield generated by the
non-pivot normalized coordinates.  Its binary extension degree controls a
Frobenius iterate fixing every coordinate, and exact periodicity will force
that degree to equal the closed-point degree.
-/

noncomputable section

namespace MazurProof.RationalPointsN25QuotientTwoClosedPointResidueDegree

